WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:04.150 align:start position:0%
 
this  is banned in kenya the government  stopped all contact sports  including football six months ago to  prevent the spread of covid19  but the kenyan premier league is hoping  for government permission to restart  next month  gord mahia football club has won it six  times in the last seven years  and the players are keen to prove  themselves again  so despite the ban they've resumed  training with some coved prevention  measures  if you can't play and the funds can't  come towards you so  it's it has been difficult and the  league had to be canceled so  we had to stay home and try and train  from home so it really affected us even  financially  the clubs did have no money not  only football has suffered because of  the covid restrictions  nearly two million kenyans have lost  their jobs  many from the poorest neighborhoods  where football is a popular pastime  community games like this one have  resumed in recent weeks  schools have been closed since march  there's not much to do  especially for young people the  coronavirus hasn't really caused the  kind of  major health crisis in kenya that people  feared might happen  relatively few people have become ill or  died compared to many other countries  and so the people here feel never mind  the rules  life and football must go on  the match organisers say it helps keep  school-aged children away from drug  abuse and crime  the league's clubs say they need to get  back in shape ahead of africa's  champions league  and qualifiers for the africa cup of  nations  here gorma are playing a friendly match  and it seems  nobody's stopping them two passing  police officers  stopped to watch the game i don't want  to say they're not enforcing it they are  enforcing it the fact that you are not  being caught you're trying as much as  possible  to comply and we see that it is right  now  that they do lift it and hopefully that  another  two days we should be prosecuted  for breaching the rules new covid rules  are expected to be announced on tuesday  the clubs and fans are hoping and  expecting that big games  will be allowed to kick off again  malcolm webb  al jazeera nairobi kenya

